Ingersoll Rand is committed to achieving workforce diversity reflective of our communities. We are an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran status, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances.

Product Marketing Manager

Location

France – Remote

About Us

For more than 100 years, professionals have relied on Ingersoll Rand for quality and performance on the toughest jobs. Our advanced engineering and manufacturing capabilities have set industry standards for excellence, reliability, and innovation. From assembly tools and industrial tools to cordless solutions and vehicle service equipment, Ingersoll Rand continues to help customers improve productivity and performance worldwide.

As part of our continued growth, we are looking for a Product Marketing Manager to drive the success of our Maintenance & Repair portfolio across the EMEIA region.

Job Summary

Reporting to the EMEIA Product Marketing Leader, you will play a key role in shaping the future of our Maintenance & Repair portfolio, including Cordless Tools.

You will be responsible for defining and executing product marketing strategies that drive growth, strengthen market position, and maximize profitability across the EMEIA region. Working closely with Sales, Product Management, Engineering, and Regional Marketing teams, you will transform customer insights into innovative product and marketing initiatives that deliver measurable business results.

Responsibilities

* Drive revenue growth, market share expansion, and profitability across the Maintenance & Repair portfolio throughout the EMEIA region;

* Define and execute product marketing strategies aligned with business objectives and growth ambitions;

* Contribute to the product roadmap and support new product development and launch activities;

* Manage the product lifecycle and ensure portfolio vitality through continuous optimization;

* Analyze market trends, customer needs, and competitive activities to identify growth opportunities

* Optimize pricing strategies to support profitability and market competitiveness;

* Develop impactful marketing content and sales enablement tools, including digital campaigns, brochures, and product launches;

* Collaborate with cross-functional teams to generate demand, improve customer engagement, and achieve commercial targets.

Basic Qualifications

* Master’s degree in Business, Marketing, Engineering, or a related field;

* Minimum 5 years of experience in Product Marketing within an industrial or technical environment;

* Proven ability to manage product portfolios and drive business growth;

* Strong analytical and strategic thinking capabilities;

* Fluent in French and English.

Travel & Work Arrangements / Requirements

This position is open to full-time remote working from anywhere in France.

Occasional travel to the Chalifert site (77) and across the EMEIA region will be required for team meetings, customer visits, product launches, training sessions, trade shows, and other business-related activities.

The successful candidate must be willing and able to travel as business needs require.

Key Competencies

* Results-oriented mindset with strong commercial acumen;

* Excellent prioritization, planning, and organizational skills;

* Strong communication, presentation, and influencing abilities;

* Ability to collaborate effectively across international and cross-functional teams;

* Customer-focused approach with a passion for innovation;

* Creative, proactive, and energetic personality.

What We Offer

* Competitive salary package

* Full remote working from anywhere in France;

* Health insurance;

* RTT;

* Ownership Works equity program: all eligible employees receive a stock grant after one year of service;

* Access to LinkedIn Learning and continuous development opportunities;

* Real career growth opportunities within a global industrial leader;

* A collaborative, innovative, and international working environment.

Ready to power the future with us?

Join Ingersoll Rand and help shape innovative solutions that drive performance for customers around the world.

